Package: syncphony-box
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Syncphony Box <madeofpendletonwool@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/madeofpendletonwool/syncphony-box
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: adduser, systemd, initramfs-tools, cage, chromium, curl, ca-certificates, avahi-daemon, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, pulseaudio-utils, network-manager, dnsmasq-base, v4l-utils, systemd-timesyncd
Description: Syncphony Box: a TV's big screen and speaker for a Syncphony room
 The software that makes a computer plugged into a TV a Syncphony box:
 boxd (the box bridge, setup and offline screens, watchdogs, HDMI-CEC and
 the Wi-Fi setup hotspot), the cage + Chromium kiosk session, the audio
 setup, the read-only root and /data machinery, and the nightly updater.
 .
 It is built for the syncphony-box image and expects that image's layout
 (the read-only root behind an overlay, /data, the boot partition with
 syncphony.txt). Installing it on an ordinary desktop is not supported.
